stork-duplicate — docker-compose.yml env addition (NOT applied here by design)
==============================================================================

Add ONE line to the `stork-capture` service's `environment:` block in
ENV2_COMPOSE/docker-compose.yml (the block currently around lines 1784-1791,
right after the existing `STORK_REORDER: "0"` line):

      STORK_DUPLICATE_TERMINAL: "0"

Resulting block (for reference — do not copy the surrounding lines, only add
the one new key):

    environment:
      STUB_PORT: "8080"
      STORK_SEED_FILE: /app/seed/subscriptions.json
      STORK_EVENTS_LOG_FILE: /data/events.jsonl
      STORK_REORDER: "0"
      STORK_DUPLICATE_TERMINAL: "0"          # <-- ADD THIS LINE
      # optional override of the terminal event set (default shown):
      # STORK_DUPLICATE_EVENTS: "payout.processed,payout.failed,payout.reversed"

Notes
-----
- Default is "0" (off) => byte-identical to the frozen baseline: exactly one
  delivery per subscription, X-Razorpay-Event-Id minted inside _deliver as
  before. Declaring the key at "0" changes NOTHING at runtime; it only makes
  the control visible/toggleable.
- Set to "1" (or "true") to have terminal payout webhooks
  (payout.processed / payout.failed / payout.reversed) delivered twice with an
  identical event_id and a byte-identical body.
- This file is a note only. Per task constraints docker-compose.yml is NOT
  edited by this change; apply the line above by hand when you want the toggle
  exposed at the compose layer.
